        ],
        [
          "içmek",
          "to drink"
        ],
        [
          "uyumak",
          "to sleep"
        ]
      ],
      "quiz": [
        {
          "q": "Which is the correct form of «I am reading»?",
          "options": [
            "okuyorum",
            "okuyorsun",
            "okuyoruz"
          ],
          "a": 0,
          "why": "The first person of the present continuous is -yorum: oku + yorum."
        },
        {
          "q": "How do you say «I am not doing»?",
          "options": [
            "yapmıyorum",
            "yapıyorum",
            "yapmıyor"
          ],
          "a": 0,
          "why": "The negative suffix -mı/-mi/-mu/-mü goes before -yor: yap-mı-yor-um."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u3",
      "num": 3,
      "level": "A1",
      "title": "Doing the shopping",
      "goal": "Use the cases of place, ask for a price and tell the time.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Three suffixes are enough to locate an action: the <b>dative</b> marks the destination («to, towards»), the <b>locative</b> the place where you are, and the <b>ablative</b> the origin («from»). They follow vowel harmony."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "The three cases of place",
          "head": [
            "Case",
            "Suffix",
            "okul (school)",
            "ev (house)",
            "sokak (street)"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Dative",
              "-(y)a / -(y)e",
              "<tur>okula</tur>",
              "<tur>eve</tur>",
              "<tur>sokağa</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "Locative",
              "-da / -de (-ta / -te)",
              "<tur>okulda</tur>",
              "<tur>evde</tur>",
              "<tur>sokakta</tur>"
            ],
            [
              "Ablative",
              "-dan / -den (-tan / -ten)",
              "<tur>okuldan</tur>",
              "<tur>evden</tur>",
              "<tur>sokaktan</tur>"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "Voiceless consonants",
          "text": "After <b>p, ç, t, k, s, ş, f, h</b>, d becomes t: <tur>sokakta</tur>, <tur>kitapta</tur>. And after a vowel, the dative takes a buffer y: <tur>masa → masaya</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "To ask the time: <tur>Saat kaç?</tur> (What time is it?). Useful answers: <tur>Saat üç.</tur> (3 o'clock), <tur>Üç buçuk.</tur> (half past three), <tur>Üçü çeyrek geçiyor.</tur> (quarter past three), <tur>Üçe çeyrek var.</tur> (quarter to three)."
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Okula gidiyorum.",
              "fr": "I am going to school."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Marketten ekmek alıyorum.",
              "fr": "I am buying bread at the market."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Kütüphanede çalışıyorum.",
              "fr": "I am working at the library."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Saat kaç? — Saat beş.",
              "fr": "What time is it? — Five o'clock."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "Calendar",
          "text": "The days and months are collected on the <a href=\"essentiel.html\">Essentials</a> page so you can review them all at once."
        }
      ],
      "vocab": [
        [
          "alışveriş",
          "shopping"
        ],
        [
          "market",
          "supermarket"
        ],
        [
          "ekmek",
