    {
      "id": "u7",
      "num": 7,
      "level": "A2",
      "title": "Possession and belonging",
      "goal": "Say what belongs to whom, form noun compounds and use var / yok.",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Possession is marked by a suffix added to the possessed noun: <b>-(i)m, -(i)n, -(s)i, -(i)miz, -(i)niz, -leri</b>. The possessor can be expressed before it, but the suffix remains obligatory."
        },
        {
          "t": "table",
          "caption": "ev (house) with possessive suffixes",
          "head": [
            "Person",
            "Form",
            "Meaning"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "benim",
              "<tur>evim</tur>",
              "my house"
            ],
            [
              "senin",
              "<tur>evin</tur>",
              "your house"
            ],
            [
              "onun",
              "<tur>evi</tur>",
              "his / her house"
            ],
            [
              "bizim",
              "<tur>evimiz</tur>",
              "our house"
            ],
            [
              "sizin",
              "<tur>eviniz</tur>",
              "your house"
            ],
            [
              "onların",
              "<tur>evleri</tur>",
              "their house"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "tip",
          "tag": "Consonants that change",
          "text": "When a suffix beginning with a vowel is added, <b>p → b</b>, <b>ç → c</b>, <b>t → d</b>, <b>k → ğ</b>: <tur>kitap → kitabım</tur>, <tur>ağaç → ağacım</tur>, <tur>sokak → sokağım</tur>."
        },
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "A noun compound links two nouns: the first takes the genitive <b>-(n)ın / -in / -un / -ün</b>, the second the possessive. <tur>Türkiye'nin başkenti</tur> (the capital of Turkey), <tur>kapı kolu</tur> (the door handle)."
        },
        {
          "t": "ex",
          "items": [
            {
              "tr": "Bu benim evim.",
              "fr": "This is my house."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Kitabım masada.",
              "fr": "My book is on the table."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Ankara, Türkiye'nin başkentidir.",
              "fr": "Ankara is the capital of Turkey."
            },
            {
              "tr": "Bugün vaktim yok.",
              "fr": "I don't have time today."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "t": "note",
          "kind": "info",
          "tag": "var / yok",
          "text": "<tur>var</tur> means «there is / has», <tur>yok</tur> «there is not». Examples: <tur>Bir arabam var.</tur> (I have a car.), <tur>Zamanım yok.</tur> (I don't have time.)."
        }
